            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Methods for recovering viable microorganisms from a sample comprising an antimicrobial agent comprise incubating the sample with coated particles to form particle-microorganism complexes and then separating the particle-microorganism complexes from the antimicrobial agent. These methods are used to detect the absence or presence of a microorganism in a sample that also contains an antimicrobial agent. Corresponding compositions and kits are also provided.</p>
            </abstract>
